# Conventional Commits: <type>(<scope>): <subject>
# types: feat | fix | docs | refactor | test | chore | build
# Subject: imperative, <= 72 chars, no trailing period.
#
# Body: what & why, wrapped at ~72 chars. Reference PRs/issues.
#
# ============ AI commit declaration (MANDATORY for AI-authored commits) ======
# If this commit is authored by an AI agent, BEFORE committing you must:
#   1. Present the declaration to the human in the session (no silent AI
#      commits), then
#   2. Uncomment and fill the block below so it lands in the commit message.
# Human authors: leave the block commented out / delete it.
#
# AI-declaration: this commit was authored by an AI agent under human direction.
# AI-agent: <agent name and model, e.g. Super Z (GLM)>
# AI-scope: <one line — exactly what the AI did in this commit>
# AI-gate: lint=pass typecheck=pass test=pass (<N> tests)
# ============================================================================
